                    briefing_text_r2:       `Before allocating a euro, set the differentiation positioning. <strong>Deepen</strong> the responsible-innovation niche, <strong>pivot</strong> to an adjacent differentiator, or <strong>broaden</strong> toward a generalist top-40 school. A credible position is defined as much by exclusions as inclusions — state explicitly <em>what MBS will not compete on</em>. Then tie the positioning to the ranking levers it does and does not help. The trap two rivals have set: matching them head-on in an arms race you cannot win, with three times your budget on the exact ground they just claimed.`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Allocate: the €14M across exec-ed, degrees, faculty and brand`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `Distribute the <strong>€14M</strong> consistent with your positioning. Concentrate a real bet rather than funding 45% of every ask. Exec-ed pays back fast and props up the surplus; degree spend fixes the money-fixable ranking drivers; faculty is slow but it is the <em>reputation engine</em> behind EQUIS and your innovation claim. <strong>Phase the spend</strong> to protect the 2.0% surplus floor — front-loading Year 1 can trip the covenant. And decide the fate of two star professors being courted by rivals, each anchoring a ~€600k chair: let them walk and you hollow out the very faculty that makes the school credible.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Defend: the board strategy session`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Present positioning, allocation and ranking response to the board chair and a sceptical trustee. They will press two challenges: <em>“you're spreading €14M too thin”</em> and <em>“you're abandoning our identity.”</em> Show the bet you chose to win and what it lets MBS do that it couldn't before; prove the allocation deepens the moat rather than contradicting the slogan; and confirm the 2.0% covenant holds. Then commit to the four KPIs the board will judge in 18–36 months: differentiation, ranking, surplus and portfolio balance.`,

