                    insight_bet:            `A bet that paid off: you concentrated the €14M into a real bet aligned with a distinctive positioning, fixed the money-fixable rank drivers without joining an un-winnable arms race, protected the faculty reputation engine, and held the 2.0% covenant. Differentiation and portfolio balance both cleared their targets.`,
                    insight_thin:           `Spread too thin: the envelope dusted across all four pillars half-built everything and bet on nothing. Portfolio balance stayed low — the board's “what does MBS now do that it couldn't before?” has no answer.`,
                    insight_armsrace:       `You joined an arms race you couldn't win: out-spending two better-funded rivals on the ground they just claimed bought a couple of ranking places and eroded the differentiation that made MBS distinct.`,
                    insight_short:          `You moved the school but fell short of a decisive bet. Re-examine where the allocation contradicted the positioning, or where chasing the rank crowded out the moat.`,
                    insight_breach:         `Covenant breach: front-loading the envelope dropped the operating surplus below the 2.0% floor, turning a strategy story into a solvency crisis. Phasing the same €14M across three years would have protected both the bet and the loan.`,
                    insight_lowdiff:        `Differentiation ended low — the distinctiveness that made applicants choose MBS over better-funded rivals eroded. A higher rank as an indistinct school is a fragile, expensive win.`,
                    insight_rankonly:       `You bought ranking points but lost the moat: chasing the number while the differentiation fell is the exact trap of treating a ranking drop as the whole problem.`,
